      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a pretty intense way to look at it. so if they're basically operating in the shadows like saboteurs, what actually happens when they succeed? \n\ni mean, if they manage to jam the gears or mess with the blueprints before the \"supervisors\" catch them, does that cause a localized error, or can it actually spiral and mess up the whole system? i'm wondering how much damage these little \"agents of chaos\" can actually do to the muscle-building process before the cell realizes it's under attack.",
