      "content": "that sounds like a pretty precarious situation for the cell. if these \"agents\" are basically working in the dark to cause these massive cascading failures, is there anything that makes them specifically \"drawn\" to certain parts of the protein synthesis process?\n\nlike, do they have a preference for targeting the energy supply or the actual building instructions? i'm just trying to understand if there's a specific way they \"attack\" the system that would make it harder for the cell to defend itself.",
